# A header's `deprecated` attribute is clang's advice to whoever names the
# name, and the compiler's own lines are nobody's choice (design.md §4.19,
# Part 8's *this language has no warning level*; panel 205's R5, ratified
# 2026-10-10; defect 571).
#
# **The compiler names every name a group binds**, in its result assertion,
# its probe, a constant's accessor, a record's field assertions and
# per-type functions, so `<ucontext.h>` bound through a header of the
# program's own defining `_XOPEN_SOURCE 600` built at exit 0 and printed
# clang's `-Wdeprecated-declarations` at the emitted `_Static_assert(
# HERO_RET_I32(getcontext((void *)0)), ...)`, a line no author wrote, over a
# correct program that never called it (panel 205's critic, `uc`).
#
# **So the warning is quiet on every line of a unit after the groups'
# close** (`emit/macro_guard.hero`), the program's own definitions as the
# compiler's assertions, probes, prototypes, prologues and accessors (panel
# 208's R1, defects 584 and 587): a deprecation is advice about a program,
# not a mistake in it, and this language has no warning level. Until then it
# was spoken again over the program's definitions, so the program's own call
# printed clang's raw text at the emitted C, and `main`'s prologue temporary
# of a group's record, a line no author wrote, did too (panel 208's
# compiler-engineer, s3). Nothing about a verdict moves: the warning was never
# an error, and a unit that binds no group's header writes none of these
# lines. A name its header marks `unavailable` is clang's error, not its
# warning, and no line here reaches it (`emit/ffi_unavailable.hero`).

constant QUIET: str
    "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wdeprecated-declarations\""

# The two groups beside it, quiet from the same close: a macro its header
# marks with `#pragma clang deprecated` (defect 587), and GCC's `warning`
# attribute, which clang says at -O0 and not at -O2, so it can carry no
# verdict (panel 208).
constant BESIDE: [str]
    [
        "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wdeprecated-pragma\""
        "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wattribute-warning\""
    ]

## Tests

test "the three lines name the three warnings, each quiet"
    assert QUIET == "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wdeprecated-declarations\""
    assert BESIDE == ["#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wdeprecated-pragma\"", "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wattribute-warning\""]
